# Upstream cadcode ignores this whole directory: there, cadpy is regenerated
# from a canonical packages/cadpy/ tree by scripts/build/build-skill-runtimes.sh,
# so a tracked copy would let source edits land in the wrong place.
#
# This is a VENDORED SNAPSHOT inside text2cad, and no such build step exists on
# panda — the installed skill is the only copy of cadpy, and it carries edits the
# pipeline depends on (checks.py's interference band, render_part.py's ambient
# and colour handling). Tracking it is the entire point of vendoring, so the
# blanket ignore is dropped here and only build artifacts stay out.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
